  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Preview 11 improves AppSourceCop compatibility validation for historical Business Central\n      baselines. Application, Platform, and explicit dependencies recorded only in the baseline\n      package are now restored, including canonical and localized Microsoft Application symbols\n      when the requested major is no longer available on NuGet. Baselines are matched by AppId,\n      allowing intentional app name or publisher changes to proceed to AppSourceCop validation.\n      Failed checks still stage the current app for dependent validations, preventing cascading\n      missing-package errors. Compiler errors are highlighted in red, warnings remain yellow,\n      workspace compilation explicitly disables report-layout generation, and all configured\n      feeds are checked before using a package below the requested version floor. Stricter\n      transitive dependency requirements now upgrade packages restored at an older direct minimum.\n      See CHANGELOG.md for full details.",
